# Binary Exploitation

### Buffer Overflow

Occurs when more data is written into a buffer than it can hold, causing adjacent memory to be overwritten.

### `gets()`

Reads user input without checking its length.
**Unsafe** because it can easily cause buffer overflows.

### `strcpy()`

Copies one string into another without checking the destination buffer size.
Can also lead to buffer overflows.

### `SIGSEGV`

A segmentation fault signal generated when a program accesses invalid memory.
In many beginner CTF challenges, this signal is intentionally handled to reveal the flag.

